# Redirects for flume.adamgreenwell.com
#
# This file must sit in the REPOSITORY ROOT, not in `dist/`. Sevalla differs
# from Netlify here, and it fails silently: a `_redirects` in the publish
# directory is simply never read, so every rule below would appear to do
# nothing while looking perfectly correct.
#
# Rules are matched top to bottom and the first hit wins, so the per-page
# mappings have to precede the catch-all at the bottom.
#
# `301!` rather than `301`. The bang forces the redirect even when a file
# exists at that path — without it a rule is skipped whenever the static build
# has something to serve there, which is exactly the case being handled if a
# stale `/docs/*` page is ever published again.
#
# Each page gets two rules: the bare path and the splat. Astro emits these
# pages in directory format, so both `/docs/user-guide` and `/docs/user-guide/`
# resolved before this change and both have to keep resolving now.

# ── documentation now lives in the GitHub Wiki ──────────────────────────────
#
# The site used to render its own copy of `flume/docs/`, which meant the same
# pages were published twice under different URLs. The wiki is the one that
# stays: it is generated from `docs/` by `wiki-sync.yml` on every push, so it
# cannot drift, and it does not need this site to be rebuilt to update.
#
# Mapped page for page rather than dumped at the wiki index. Someone arriving
# from a search result for a specific page should land on that page, and a
# mapped 301 passes the ranking those URLs already have.

/docs/getting-started            https://github.com/adamgreenwell/flume/wiki/Getting-Started         301!
/docs/getting-started/*          https://github.com/adamgreenwell/flume/wiki/Getting-Started         301!
/docs/user-guide                 https://github.com/adamgreenwell/flume/wiki/User-Guide              301!
/docs/user-guide/*               https://github.com/adamgreenwell/flume/wiki/User-Guide              301!
/docs/architecture               https://github.com/adamgreenwell/flume/wiki/Architecture            301!
/docs/architecture/*             https://github.com/adamgreenwell/flume/wiki/Architecture            301!
/docs/torrent-engine-notes       https://github.com/adamgreenwell/flume/wiki/Torrent-Engine-Notes    301!
/docs/torrent-engine-notes/*     https://github.com/adamgreenwell/flume/wiki/Torrent-Engine-Notes    301!
/docs/design-system              https://github.com/adamgreenwell/flume/wiki/Design-System           301!
/docs/design-system/*            https://github.com/adamgreenwell/flume/wiki/Design-System           301!
/docs/development-setup          https://github.com/adamgreenwell/flume/wiki/Development-Setup       301!
/docs/development-setup/*        https://github.com/adamgreenwell/flume/wiki/Development-Setup       301!
/docs/ci-cd-and-releases         https://github.com/adamgreenwell/flume/wiki/CI-CD-and-Releases      301!
/docs/ci-cd-and-releases/*       https://github.com/adamgreenwell/flume/wiki/CI-CD-and-Releases      301!
/docs/signing-and-distribution   https://github.com/adamgreenwell/flume/wiki/Signing-and-Distribution 301!
/docs/signing-and-distribution/* https://github.com/adamgreenwell/flume/wiki/Signing-and-Distribution 301!
/docs/privacy                    https://github.com/adamgreenwell/flume/wiki/Privacy                 301!
/docs/privacy/*                  https://github.com/adamgreenwell/flume/wiki/Privacy                 301!
/docs/platform-notes             https://github.com/adamgreenwell/flume/wiki/Platform-Notes          301!
/docs/platform-notes/*           https://github.com/adamgreenwell/flume/wiki/Platform-Notes          301!
/docs/smoke-test-checklist       https://github.com/adamgreenwell/flume/wiki/Smoke-Test-Checklist    301!
/docs/smoke-test-checklist/*     https://github.com/adamgreenwell/flume/wiki/Smoke-Test-Checklist    301!
/docs/roadmap                    https://github.com/adamgreenwell/flume/wiki/Roadmap                 301!
/docs/roadmap/*                  https://github.com/adamgreenwell/flume/wiki/Roadmap                 301!

# Anything else under /docs, including the index and any page retired from the
# wiki, lands on the wiki home rather than a 404.
/docs                            https://github.com/adamgreenwell/flume/wiki                         301!
/docs/*                          https://github.com/adamgreenwell/flume/wiki                         301!

# ── custom 404 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Sevalla's "Error file" build setting does not do this. Its documentation is
# explicit that Index file and Error file are for single-page applications —
# they route all navigation through one file — and setting Error file on a
# multi-page site was verified to change nothing, even after a redeploy. The
# SPA route is also the one to avoid: it serves the home page under every wrong
# URL with a 200 and tells search engines each of them is real.
#
# This rule is the Netlify idiom and Sevalla honours the same file. It must be
# LAST, because the first match wins and it matches everything.
#
# Deliberately NOT forced. Without the bang a rule only applies when no file
# exists at that path, so every real page still serves itself and only genuine
# misses fall through here — with a 404 status rather than a 200, which is the
# whole point.
/*                               /404.html                                    404

